>   Does this sound like a bug to y'all?  If you have a blessed luckstone,
>   place it into a sack that you are carrying and then drink a potion of
>   enlightenment, it does not show you as having any modifiers to luck.
>   Should you lose the benefits of carrying an item just because it is 
>   carried in a sack?
>	   Note that luckstones (and possibly a few more objects) are 
>   fairly unique in that all you have to do to reap the benefits is to
>   carry them (i.e., not wield, wear, etc.).

	hmm.  The archaeologist quest artifact, the Orb of Detection, gives
the carrier telepathy only if it's uncursed and carried outside a bag.
The same applies to luckstones and some other quest items, i think.
Not to mention the bell, book and candelabrum, none of which work when
cursed and none of which can be confined in bags.
	I guess this should logically qualify as a bug, as it seems
strange that just putting an artifact in a bag could cancel its
magical effects.  However, fixing this "bug" might make the game far
too easy.  There should be some incentive to carry powerful artifacts
outside a bag, where they can be cursed by liches, etc.  

